00:11:15.301 --> 00:11:20.401
To really understand a diplomatic break, separate the person at the embassy from the paper that

00:11:20.401 --> 00:11:25.761
binds two states. People hear that an ambassador was sent home and picture a treaty ripped up.

00:11:25.761 --> 00:11:31.321
That mixes three acts, and this next stretch is my own explanation of the mechanism, not

00:11:31.321 --> 00:11:32.881
a finding from today's reporting.

00:11:33.641 --> 00:11:36.321
Under the Vienna practice, most capital still follow.

00:11:36.781 --> 00:11:42.481
A host country can declare a diplomat persona non-grata, no longer welcome, and the sending

00:11:42.481 --> 00:11:44.641
country is expected to pull that person out.

00:11:45.161 --> 00:11:49.561
The embassy as an office can stay, sometimes under a lower ranking stand-in.

00:11:50.041 --> 00:11:52.601
Calling your own ambassador home is the matching move.

00:11:52.601 --> 00:11:56.581
you remove your representative without automatically shutting the building or

00:11:56.581 --> 00:12:01.261
stopping trade. Cancelling a name, defense deal, or a commercial contract is a

00:12:01.261 --> 00:12:06.241
third act, and it has to name the contract. Diplomats can also have been gone for

00:12:06.241 --> 00:12:10.821
months before any expulsion order, so the public rupture and the empty desk need

00:12:10.821 --> 00:12:15.641
not be the same day. When you next see an expulsion lead the news, look for a

00:12:15.641 --> 00:12:19.561
separate list of canceled agreements. If that list is missing, the legal

00:12:19.561 --> 00:12:21.661
relationship has not been described yet.

